WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:01.668
What is the danger,

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.837
do you think, in the months ahead?

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:05.338
Given the first issue,

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.540
which is the seemingly relentless

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.542
drawdown of weapons from the U.S.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:10.944
and other natal countries,

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:11.244
you know,

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.846
as this war continues

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:13.413
to draw down

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:14.314
on more and more

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:16.683
stockpiles and equipment.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:17.350
Yeah, Paula,

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.251
that's one of the

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:19.052
big issues

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:19.886
that's confronting

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.888
the entire Western alliance,

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.757
because the defense industrial base,

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:25.125
as it's known

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.459
of all these countries,

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.094
the natal countries in Europe,

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:30.697
as well as the United States and Canada,

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:31.965
it's really not built

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.466
for this kind of war.

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.201
And that very fact has made

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.503
it really difficult

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:39.806
for the West to resupply Ukraine

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:41.408
Ukraine is using weapons

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:43.076
that are very high rate.

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:44.044
It's using ammunition,

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:45.378
of course, as part of this.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:46.413
And then the other thing

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:47.280
that we're confronted

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.483
with is the barrels of the various

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.719
artillery pieces that are overheating

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.587
because of overuse.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:56.589
So that's a major issue for

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.024
the Ukrainians

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:58.892
and for the West,

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.927
especially if the West wants to continue

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.028
to help the Ukrainians,

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.063
then help the Ukrainians

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:03.930
stop the Russians.

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:06.032
You know, Secretary of

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.200
State Antony Blinken spoke

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.134
to CNN's

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.903
Christiane Amanpour about the option

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:10.737
we were just talking

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.072
about the right of possibly

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:15.275
resuscitating Soviet era weapons systems.

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:16.709
I never thought I would hear this

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.711
after hearing for more than three decades

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:19.846
that the West wanted

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.114
these Eastern European countries

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:22.615
to modernize their military.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:23.750
But I want you to listen to them now.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.618
We'll talk on the back end

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:27.821
we're looking at

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:30.557
at every option to make sure that, again,

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.358
they get what they need

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.494
and what can be most effective for them.

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:36.329
Some of that does go to

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:37.530
Soviet era systems

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.866
that they've had in their inventory

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:40.500
for decades.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.201
And, for example,

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:42.469
making sure that the

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:43.603
ammunition is there

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:46.072
for those for those systems.

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:46.673
So, Colonel,

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:47.474
does this strike you

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:49.142
as a good strategic option

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:50.543
or more of a sign

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:51.811
of desperation

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:52.445
that, you know,

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.313
there has been a study,

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.581
the most recent from the Center

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:56.449
for Strategic and International Studies

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.050
and found

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:00.520
that it would take years to replenish

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.221
these stocks,

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:02.355
given that, as you say,

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.256
the industrial

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:04.157
industrial military

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:06.092
complex is designed for peace

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:06.993
I mean, does

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:07.460
it strike

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.562
you as desperate or a creative idea?

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:12.765
Well, it's somewhat creative in the sense

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:13.766
that the Ukrainians,

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:15.502
of course, have had this Soviet

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:17.804
era weapon systems ever since they gained

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:21.241
they regained their independence in 1991.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.143
So they're used to this,

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:24.911
they've been trained on this

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.379
and even if they've had a break

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:27.447
in service

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:29.582
between their initial military service

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:32.252
and their call up for this war,

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.887
they're still familiar with these

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:34.954
with these weapon systems.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.122
So in that sense,

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:38.291
it makes sense to do that.

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:40.226
But on the other hand,

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.328
these systems are old.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:43.763
They are not as effective

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:45.365
as their Western counterparts.

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:46.232
Especially the modern

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:47.600
Western counterparts.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.502
And the Ukrainians

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:50.703
would be better served

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:53.306
if they could receive the Western systems

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.141
and they could be trained on them

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.643
so that's the big end.

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:57.744
But that is one of the key

00:02:57.744 --> 00:02:58.511
things that

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:59.879
would need to happen in this case.

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.080
So I think it requires

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.149
a lot of creative solutions.

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:05.418
You know, using the old Soviet equipment

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:07.320
but also ramping up the training

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:10.490
for modern Western equipment to be used

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.625
by the Ukrainians themselves. Right.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.327
So you look a two track approach

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:15.195
that you're talking about.

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:16.863
I'm going to lean on your expertize here,

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:17.730
because we all remember

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.598
at the start of this war

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:19.999
that Ukraine asked for that

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:21.834
no fly zone that they didn't get.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.937
Now, you say it's now highly likely

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.071
that these new air

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.339
defense systems

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:28.841
that they get maybe could potentially

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:30.577
have a truly integrated

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:31.911
air and missile defense system in

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:32.745
place for Ukraine.

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:34.981
Do you think though, that

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.449
it will come soon enough?

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:37.450
Given everything you've seen

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:38.952
on the battlefield?

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:39.586
Yeah, that's

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:40.753
my biggest concern,

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:41.654
Paula, actually,

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.189
that they won't come soon enough.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:45.225
So this requires

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:46.759
not only the logistical piece

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:47.527
to move forward,

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:48.728
but also the training piece

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:49.796
to move forward.

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:53.833
And we do understand that the U.S.

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:54.934
is working

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.836
in conjunction with the Ukrainians

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:58.671
and with NATO's partners,

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:00.173
especially Germany,

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:02.642
to train a much greater volume

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:05.745
of Ukrainians on Western systems.

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:09.115
So if that happens, I it can be done,

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:11.117
but it also requires the Ukrainians

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:12.218
to leave their country

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:14.053
and leave their fighting posts

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:15.855
in order to come in and get some training

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:17.523
and then come back.

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:18.658
So it's a

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:20.693
it's a bit of a tough haul, and it's

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:22.528
certainly very concerning.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.764
And basically the clock is running out

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.266
in multiple directions.

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:27.166
And that's going to be

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.434
a really big

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.136
problem for the West,

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:32.105
for the Ukrainians and

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:33.039
really for the world.

